comment=DT-HOLD-90 v4 -- ONE word: the helper's kind-8 attachment holds 76-89 ticks.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// R6a. v3 after the five-lane hostile review (docs/dt-hold-90-review/).
//
//   201ef918  2403001e -> 2403005a   addiu v1, zero, 30 -> 90
//
// Site A's kind-7/8 band copy. Lane 1 proved the band exact (only {7,8} reach
// it; new kind unconditionally 8), the value flow clean, and the timer range
// 76..89 ticks from measured ratings (+0xB86/+0xB88 = PPBK/PRBK, 38..229).
// Kind 7 is NOT initialised elsewhere as v2 claimed -- the SAME store stamps
// it, but with ZERO via the daddu-zero idiom at 0x001ef88c, so the up-counter
// always starts at 0 and review-D5's self-defeat cannot occur.
//
// v2's second word (201f2108, Site B) is REMOVED: lane 2 proved that stamp is
// a 16-frame REFRESH (defender +0x42C := 16 gates re-stamping), so the
// primary's kind-4 timer never underflows at 30 or 90 -- the word bought
// nothing. The pairing is bound solely by the helper's kind-8 timer above.
//
// v2's 0x001ca0e8 slti-61 warning is WITHDRAWN: lanes 1 and 3 independently
// proved that block is gated `bne v1, 3` -- kind-3 only, unreachable for
// kinds 4/8. Lane 3's closed census (13 readers) found NO comparison that
// 76-89 crosses and 15-30 does not.
//
// Pass plays: on the measured 7<->8 oscillation the timer is re-stamped each
// 7->8 and re-zeroed each 8->7, so the patch is INERT there (lane 3). Slot 7
// regression run retained as confirmation.
//
// Encoding v4 (lane 5): `word` type, PROVEN 32-bit in this fork from repo
// history (protocol-notes.md:212's working .text patch), instead of leading-2
// `extended`, which is UNVERIFIED here. The 30->90 delta is low-byte-only so
// the risk was low either way; `word` removes it entirely.
//
// EXECUTION PROOF (lane 5's T4, stronger than a memory read-back): sample the
// helper's +0x432 during the run. Baseline initialisation cannot exceed 30,
// so any read >= 61 proves the patched immediate EXECUTED through the
// recompiler -- settling the cache question the dt44 null result could not
// (lane 5 showed 0x001f6b08 branches past that word for state-2 defenders,
// so dt44 discriminated nothing).
//
// Acceptance vs slot 9 frozen-seed baseline (operator pre-registered:
// hold + outcome): dt_last_hold_frame 43 -> well past (~120+ if the helper
// holds 76-89 from lock-in ~frame 27); carrier_yards -0.70 -> moves; operator
// sees linemen STAYING on the double. R5 arm: slot 6 (dt_detect it first).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

